IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ea-core`

-- Employment (Retrenchment Reporting) Notification 2019 (S 200/2019), made under section 96A(1) of the Employment
-- Act 1968 -- informal consolidation, version in force from 1/11/2021 -- LAYER 1.  Part ea2.
-- Source text: inputs/EmA1968-S200-2019.txt (a converter rendering, not the official text).  The brief's Scope puts this
-- Notification in ea2's range; PLAN.md section 1 says "the lead must confirm"; the brief governs.
--
-- Notes for the reader.
--   * Seam S12: `S 200/2019 para 3(1) the Notification applies to the employer` and `S 200/2019 the employer met every
--     requirement concerning the report` feed `s 96A the employer failed to comply with a requirement in the notification`.
--   * The Notification has its own "working day" (para 2(1)): not a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday.  Its text governs
--     para 4, not Interpretation Act s 50(d).
--   * A plain BOOLEAN or NUMBER answer is a date or count comparison and carries no legal "no".
--   * The definition of "employer" in para 2(1) is followed by "[Deleted by S 781/2021 wef 01/11/2021]": it is read as deleted
--     (the 10-employee threshold is gone from para 3(1)).  Para 2(3) still speaks of an employer "with 10 or more employees"; it is
--     encoded as it reads, and NOTES.md finding records that nothing in the Notification now uses it.

§ `Notification -- citation, definitions and the employees it refers to (paras 1 and 2)`

-- para 1: "This Notification ... comes into operation on 1 April 2019."
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:24 | 1. This Notification is the Employment (Retrenchment Reporting)
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:25 | Notification 2019 and comes into operation on 1 April 2019.
@ref para 1 (src:EmA1968-S200-2019:24-25)
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 200/2019 para 1 the Notification is in operation on the day` MEANS
    `the day` AT LEAST (Date 1 4 2019)

-- para 2(1) "retrench": "in relation to an employee, means to terminate the employee's contract of service at the
-- initiative of the employer because of redundancy or any reorganisation of the employer's profession, business, trade or work".
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:30 | “retrench”, in relation to an employee, means to terminate the
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:31 | employee’s contract of service at the initiative of the
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:32 | employer because of redundancy or any reorganisation of
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:33 | the employer ’s profession, business, trade or work;
@ref para 2(1) "retrench" (src:EmA1968-S200-2019:30-33)
GIVEN `the employer terminated the employee's contract of service at the initiative of the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reason was redundancy or a reorganisation of the employer's profession, business, trade or work` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`S 200/2019 para 2(1) "retrench" the termination is a retrenchment` MEANS
    IF `the employer terminated the employee's contract of service at the initiative of the employer`
       AND `the reason was redundancy or a reorganisation of the employer's profession, business, trade or work`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means to terminate the"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- para 2(1) "retrenchment report": "a report required by this Notification to be given by an employer to the Commissioner
-- containing the information about the retrenchment of any employee by that employer".
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:36 | “retrenchment report ” means a report required by this
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:37 | Notification to be given by an employer to the
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:38 | Commissioner containing the information about the
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:39 | retrenchment of any employee by that employer;
@ref para 2(1) "retrenchment report" (src:EmA1968-S200-2019:36-39)
GIVEN `the report is required by this Notification to be given by an employer to the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report contains the information about the retrenchment of an employee by that employer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`S 200/2019 para 2(1) "retrenchment report" the report is one` MEANS
    IF `the report is required by this Notification to be given by an employer to the Commissioner`
       AND `the report contains the information about the retrenchment of an employee by that employer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a report required by this Notification to be given by an employer to the"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- para 2(1) "working day": "a day other than a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday".  A pure date test.
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:40 | “working day ” means a day other than a Saturday, Sunday or
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:41 | public holiday.
@ref para 2(1) "working day" (src:EmA1968-S200-2019:40-41)
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 200/2019 para 2(1) "working day" the day is one` MEANS
    `Weekday of` `the day` AT LEAST 1 AND `Weekday of` `the day` AT MOST 5 AND NOT (elem `the day` `the public holidays`)

-- para 2(2): "In this Notification, any reference to an employee is a reference to an employee who has or works under a
-- contract of service (whenever made) (a) that does not specify an end date for the contract; or (b) that has a term of
-- employment of at least 6 months."
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:42 | (2) In this Notification, any reference to an employee is a reference
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:43 | to an employee who has or works under a contract of service
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:44 | (whenever made) —
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:45 | (a) that does not specify an end date for the contract; or
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:46 | (b) that has a term of employment of at least 6 months.
@ref para 2(2) (src:EmA1968-S200-2019:42-46)
GIVEN `the contract of service specifies an end date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the term of employment in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`S 200/2019 para 2(2) the employee is one to whom the Notification refers` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the contract of service specifies an end date`) OR `the term of employment in months` AT LEAST 6
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any reference to an employee is a reference to an employee who has or works under a"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- para 2(3): "Whether or not an employer has 10 or more employees is to be worked out as at the time when a notice of
-- retrenchment is given by the employer to an employee who becomes retrenched, regardless when the notice takes effect."
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:47 | (3) Whether or not an employer has 10 or more employees is to be
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:48 | worked out as at the time when a notice of retrenchment is given by
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:49 | the employer to an employee who becomes retrenched, regardless
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:50 | when the notice takes effect.
@ref para 2(3) (src:EmA1968-S200-2019:47-50)
GIVEN `the number of employees the employer has at the time the notice of retrenchment is given` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 200/2019 para 2(3) the employer has 10 or more employees` MEANS
    `the number of employees the employer has at the time the notice of retrenchment is given` AT LEAST 10

§ `Notification -- the retrenchment report, its time and its form (paras 3 to 5)`

-- para 3(1): "Every employer must give to the Commissioner a retrenchment report in accordance with sub-paragraph (2) if, on
-- or after 1 November 2021, the employer gives any of its employees a notice of his or her retrenchment, regardless when the
-- notice takes effect or when the employment ends."
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:52 | 3.—(1) Every employer must give to the Commissioner a
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:53 | retrenchment report in accordance with sub-paragraph (2) if, on or
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:54 | after 1 November 2021, the employer gives any of its employees a
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:55 | notice of his or her retrenchment, regardless when the notice takes
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:56 | effect or when the employment ends.
@ref para 3(1) (src:EmA1968-S200-2019:52-56)
GIVEN `the day the employer gave the notice of retrenchment` IS A DATE
      `the answer of para 2(1) "retrench"` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of para 2(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`S 200/2019 para 3(1) the Notification applies to the employer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "or after 1 November 2021, the employer gives any of its employees a"
        IF `the day the employer gave the notice of retrenchment` LESS THAN (Date 1 11 2021) THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "or after 1 November 2021, the employer gives any of its employees a"
        IF `the answer of para 2(1) "retrench"` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any reference to an employee is a reference to an employee who has or works under a"
        IF `the answer of para 2(2)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the answer of para 2(1) "retrench"` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the answer of para 2(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the termination is a retrenchment, or the employee is one to whom the Notification refers, was not answered
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- The other reading of the headcount (fork F20).  The definition of "employer" at paragraph 2(1) ("an
-- employer with 10 or more employees") is followed in the rendering by "[Deleted by S 781/2021 wef
-- 01/11/2021]", and paragraph 3(1), as it stands from that day, says "Every employer".  The rule above
-- reads the definition as deleted, so the headcount of paragraph 2(3) does no work in paragraph 3(1).
-- This rule reads the definition as still operating, so that "employer" in paragraph 3(1) means an
-- employer with 10 or more employees, counted as paragraph 2(3) says: at the time the notice of
-- retrenchment is given.  It is the rule above with that threshold added.
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:52 | 3.—(1) Every employer must give to the Commissioner a
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:53 | retrenchment report in accordance with sub-paragraph (2) if, on or
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:54 | after 1 November 2021, the employer gives any of its employees a
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:55 | notice of his or her retrenchment, regardless when the notice takes
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:56 | effect or when the employment ends.
@ref para 3(1) (src:EmA1968-S200-2019:52-56)
GIVEN `the number of employees the employer has at the time the notice of retrenchment is given` IS A NUMBER
      `the day the employer gave the notice of retrenchment` IS A DATE
      `the answer of para 2(1) "retrench"` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of para 2(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`S 200/2019 para 3(1) the Notification applies to the employer, if the 10-employee definition still operates` MEANS
    IF NOT (`S 200/2019 para 2(3) the employer has 10 or more employees` `the number of employees the employer has at the time the notice of retrenchment is given`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“employer” means an employer with 10 or more employees;"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE `S 200/2019 para 3(1) the Notification applies to the employer` `the day the employer gave the notice of retrenchment` `the answer of para 2(1) "retrench"` `the answer of para 2(2)`

-- The information the Schedule specifies, item by item.  "including the following" opens each list, so the list of the
-- Schedule's own items is not closed.
DECLARE `S 200/2019 Schedule item` IS ONE OF
    `S 200/2019 sch 1(a)(i) the name and address of an employer who is an individual`
    `S 200/2019 sch 1(a)(ii)(A) the name and address of an employer who is not an individual, as on a register or official record`
    `S 200/2019 sch 1(a)(ii)(B) the name in which the employer employed the employee and the address of its principal place of business`
    `S 200/2019 sch 1(b) the trade name if different`
    `S 200/2019 sch 1(c) the nature of the profession, business, trade or work`
    `S 200/2019 sch 1(d) the registered trade union recognised, and whether it was consulted`
    `S 200/2019 sch 1(e) the particulars of the contact person`
    `S 200/2019 sch 1(f) the number of retrenched employees`
    `S 200/2019 sch 1(g) the number of employees on the date of the notice, by citizens, permanent residents and foreigners`
    `S 200/2019 sch 2(a) the name and the identity or foreign identification number`
    `S 200/2019 sch 2(b) the job title`
    `S 200/2019 sch 2(c) whether a citizen, a permanent resident or a foreigner`
    `S 200/2019 sch 2(d) the date the notice of retrenchment is given`
    `S 200/2019 sch 2(e) the effective date of retrenchment`
    `S 200/2019 sch 2(f) the retrenchment benefits paid or to be paid`
    `S 200/2019 sch 2(g) the reasons for not paying retrenchment benefits`
    `S 200/2019 sch 2(h) the employment facilitation assistance provided or to be provided`

-- Schedule item 1(a): "the name and address of the employer (i) for an employer who is an individual ...; and (ii) for an
-- employer who is not an individual (A) as specified on any register or official record kept under any written law; or (B)
-- where sub-paragraph (A) is not applicable, the name in which the employer employed the retrenched employee and the address
-- of the principal place of business".  Item 1(b): "the employer's trade name if different"; item 2(g): "if no retrenchment
-- benefits were paid ..., the reasons for not paying so".  Which items the report must state depends on three facts.
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:75 | 1. Details relating to the employer of an employee to whom a notice of
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:76 | retrenchment is given (called in this Schedule a retrenched employee),
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:77 | including the following:
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:78 | (a) the name and address of the employer —
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:79 | (i) for an employer who is an individual, as specified on the
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:80 | identity card or passport of the employer; and
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:81 | (ii) for an employer who is not an individual —
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:82 | (A) as specified on any register or official record kept under
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:83 | any written law; or
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:84 | (B) where sub-paragraph (A) is not applicable, the name in
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:85 | which the employer employed the retrenched employee
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:86 | and the address of the principal place of business of the
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:87 | employer;
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:88 | (b) the employer ’s trade name if different from that in sub-paragraph ( a);
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:89 | (c) the nature of the profession, business, trade or work carried on by the
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:90 | employer;
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:91 | (d) the name of any trade union registered under the Trade Unions Act
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:92 | (Cap. 333) recognised by the employer under the Industrial Relations
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:93 | (Recognition of a Trade Union of Employees) Regulations (Cap. 136,
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:94 | Rg 3), and whether that trade union was consulted on the retrenchment
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:95 | of one or more retrenched employees;
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:96 | (e) the particulars of the contact person of the employer;
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:97 | (f) the number of retrenched employees who are the subject of the
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:98 | retrenchment report;
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:99 | (g) the number of employees of the employer on the date the notice of
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:100 | retrenchment is given, including a breakdown of the number of
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:103 | THE SCHEDULE — continued
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:104 | citizens of Singapore, the number of permanent residents of Singapore
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:105 | and the number of foreigners.
@ref sch item 1 (src:EmA1968-S200-2019:75-105)
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:107 | 2. Details of each retrenched employee, including the following:
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:108 | (a) the name of the retrenched employee as specified on the retrenched
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:108 | (a) the name of the retrenched employee as specified on the retrenched
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:109 | employee’s identity card or work pass, and the identity card number or
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:110 | foreign identification number (as the case may be) of the retrenched
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:111 | employee;
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:112 | (b) the job title of the retrenched employee immediately before the notice
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:113 | of retrenchment was given;
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:114 | (c) whether the retrenched employee is a citizen of Singapore, a
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:115 | permanent resident of Singapore or a foreigner;
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:116 | (d) the date the notice of retrenchment is given to the employee;
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:118 | (e) the effective date of retrenchment;
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:119 | (f) the retrenchment benefits paid or to be paid to the retrenched
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:120 | employee;
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:121 | (g) if no retrenchment benefits were paid to the retrenched employee, the
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:122 | reasons for not paying so;
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:123 | (h) the employment facilitation assistance provided or to be provided to
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:124 | the retrenched employee.
@ref sch item 2 (src:EmA1968-S200-2019:107-124)
GIVEN `the employer is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the name is specified on a register or official record kept under a written law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer's trade name differs from the name in item 1(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no retrenchment benefits were paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `S 200/2019 Schedule item`
`S 200/2019 Schedule the items the report must state` MEANS
    append
        (IF `the employer is an individual`
         THEN LIST `S 200/2019 sch 1(a)(i) the name and address of an employer who is an individual`
         ELSE
            IF `the name is specified on a register or official record kept under a written law`
            THEN LIST `S 200/2019 sch 1(a)(ii)(A) the name and address of an employer who is not an individual, as on a register or official record`
            ELSE LIST `S 200/2019 sch 1(a)(ii)(B) the name in which the employer employed the employee and the address of its principal place of business`)
        (append
            (IF `the employer's trade name differs from the name in item 1(a)` THEN LIST `S 200/2019 sch 1(b) the trade name if different` ELSE EMPTY)
            (append
                (IF `no retrenchment benefits were paid` THEN LIST `S 200/2019 sch 2(g) the reasons for not paying retrenchment benefits` ELSE EMPTY)
                (LIST
                    `S 200/2019 sch 1(c) the nature of the profession, business, trade or work`,
                    `S 200/2019 sch 1(d) the registered trade union recognised, and whether it was consulted`,
                    `S 200/2019 sch 1(e) the particulars of the contact person`,
                    `S 200/2019 sch 1(f) the number of retrenched employees`,
                    `S 200/2019 sch 1(g) the number of employees on the date of the notice, by citizens, permanent residents and foreigners`,
                    `S 200/2019 sch 2(a) the name and the identity or foreign identification number`,
                    `S 200/2019 sch 2(b) the job title`,
                    `S 200/2019 sch 2(c) whether a citizen, a permanent resident or a foreigner`,
                    `S 200/2019 sch 2(d) the date the notice of retrenchment is given`,
                    `S 200/2019 sch 2(e) the effective date of retrenchment`,
                    `S 200/2019 sch 2(f) the retrenchment benefits paid or to be paid`,
                    `S 200/2019 sch 2(h) the employment facilitation assistance provided or to be provided`)))

-- A helper: every item in the required list is in the stated list.
GIVEN required IS A LIST OF `S 200/2019 Schedule item`
      stated IS A LIST OF `S 200/2019 Schedule item`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 200/2019 Schedule helper: every required item is stated` MEANS
    CONSIDER required
    WHEN EMPTY THEN TRUE
    WHEN item FOLLOWED BY rest THEN elem item stated AND `S 200/2019 Schedule helper: every required item is stated` rest stated

-- para 3(2): "The retrenchment report by the employer must contain all the information specified in the Schedule in relation to
-- the employee who is given a notice of retrenchment by the employer."  A report that leaves out an item the Schedule lists
-- does not contain all the information; a report with every listed item is not shown to be complete, because each list begins
-- "including the following".
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:57 | (2) The retrenchment report by the employer must contain all the
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:58 | information specified in the Schedule in relation to the employee who
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:59 | is given a notice of retrenchment by the employer.
@ref para 3(2) (src:EmA1968-S200-2019:57-59)
GIVEN required IS A LIST OF `S 200/2019 Schedule item`
      stated IS A LIST OF `S 200/2019 Schedule item`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`S 200/2019 para 3(2) the report contains all the information specified in the Schedule` MEANS
    IF `S 200/2019 Schedule helper: every required item is stated` required stated
    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): every item the Schedule lists is stated, but each list says "including the following", so other information may be specified
    THEN NOTHING
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must contain all the information specified in the Schedule in relation to"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- para 4: "Every retrenchment report must be given to the Commissioner not later than 5 working days after the day that the
-- employer gives the notice of retrenchment mentioned in paragraph 3."  The 5th working day after the day the notice is given.
-- A working day is the Notification's own (para 2(1)).
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:62 | 4. Every retrenchment report must be given to the Commissioner
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:63 | not later than 5 working days after the day that the employer gives the
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:64 | notice of retrenchment mentioned in paragraph 3.
@ref para 4 (src:EmA1968-S200-2019:62-64)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      n IS A NUMBER
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`S 200/2019 para 4 helper: the nth working day after` MEANS
    IF n AT MOST 0
    THEN d
    ELSE
        IF `S 200/2019 para 2(1) "working day" the day is one` (d PLUS 1) `the public holidays`
        THEN `S 200/2019 para 4 helper: the nth working day after` (d PLUS 1) (n MINUS 1) `the public holidays`
        ELSE `S 200/2019 para 4 helper: the nth working day after` (d PLUS 1) n `the public holidays`

@ref para 4 (src:EmA1968-S200-2019:62-64)
GIVEN `the day the employer gave the notice of retrenchment` IS A DATE
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`S 200/2019 para 4 the last day for giving the retrenchment report` MEANS
    `S 200/2019 para 4 helper: the nth working day after` `the day the employer gave the notice of retrenchment` 5 `the public holidays`

@ref para 4 (src:EmA1968-S200-2019:62-64)
GIVEN `the day the retrenchment report was given` IS A DATE
      `the day the employer gave the notice of retrenchment` IS A DATE
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 200/2019 para 4 the retrenchment report was given in time` MEANS
    `the day the retrenchment report was given` AT MOST `S 200/2019 para 4 the last day for giving the retrenchment report` `the day the employer gave the notice of retrenchment` `the public holidays`

-- para 5: "Every retrenchment report must be in the form provided at the website of the Ministry of Manpower ... unless the
-- Commissioner allows otherwise in any particular case."
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:69 | 5. Every retrenchment report must be in the form provided at the
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:70 | website of the Ministry of Manpower at http://www.mom.gov.sg,
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:71 | unless the Commissioner allows otherwise in any particular case.
@ref para 5 (src:EmA1968-S200-2019:69-71)
GIVEN `the report is in the form provided at the website of the Ministry of Manpower` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner has allowed otherwise in this case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`S 200/2019 para 5 the requirement as to the form of the report is met` MEANS
    IF `the report is in the form provided at the website of the Ministry of Manpower` OR `the Commissioner has allowed otherwise in this case`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the Commissioner allows otherwise in any particular case"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- Seam S12 (with s 96A): the employer met every requirement concerning the report: it did not, if the report leaves out an
-- item the Schedule lists (para 3(2)), was not given in time (para 4), or is not in the form (para 5).  Where none of these
-- is shown, the Notification does not say that the employer met its requirements.
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:52 | 3.—(1) Every employer must give to the Commissioner a
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:53 | retrenchment report in accordance with sub-paragraph (2) if, on or
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:54 | after 1 November 2021, the employer gives any of its employees a
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:55 | notice of his or her retrenchment, regardless when the notice takes
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:56 | effect or when the employment ends.
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:57 | (2) The retrenchment report by the employer must contain all the
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:58 | information specified in the Schedule in relation to the employee who
-- src:EmA1968-S200-2019:59 | is given a notice of retrenchment by the employer.
